{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects","id":1561098,"title":"Merged Beast and Lair-based atavisms effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-29T08:46:50-07:00","id":1561098,"title":"Merged Beast and Lair-based atavisms effects","content":"So, since they do not have anymore lair when a beast becomes rampant, how do they calculate the lair for the atavisms, like Looming presence? Do they count the one you had at the moment of a merger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T09:31:33-07:00","id":1561099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects#post1561098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since they do not have anymore lair when a beast becomes rampant, how do they calculate the lair for the atavisms, like Looming presence? Do they count the one you had at the moment of a merger?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes to the latter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T11:17:58-07:00","id":1561104,"title":"","content":"At this point they're not so much a Beast in the rules sense, but a unique denizen of the Dream. I'd say the best approach is to discard the rules and focus on the particular case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T16:29:02-07:00","id":1561115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects?p=1561104#post1561104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point they're not so much a Beast in the rules sense, but a unique denizen of the Dream. I'd say the best approach is to discard the rules and focus on the particular case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Madolgio is asking about the Rampant, who are physical monsters whose Horrors have filled their bodies with the collapse of their Lair; you may be thinking of their opposite numbers among the Unfettered, who are ephemeral beings.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also go with the Beast's former Lair rating for Atavisms that reference Lair, since that's already what the &quot;Body Warp&quot; Merger effect draws on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T06:45:26-07:00","id":1561134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects?p=1561115#post1561115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Madolgio is asking about the Rampant, who are physical monsters whose Horrors have filled their bodies with the collapse of their Lair; you may be thinking of their opposite numbers among the Unfettered, who are ephemeral beings.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was uncertain, but went on because I think it still applies.<br /> <br /> The Lair is relevant because it draws on certain kinds of symbolism that is important to the Beast.<br /> <br /> But when the Horror changes from Beast to something else, anything else, this is a conceptual change in a highly semantic being. Even if their Lair is relevant to say where you're coming from, I'm not sure it should inform a lot on what &quot;you&quot; become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T11:51:42-07:00","id":1561140,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that the Rampant still get Atavisms to represent them becoming physical monsters. An Eshmaki that goes Rampant and becomes a dragon flying around and hunting things gets to keep the ability to breath fire (assuming they had said Atavism).<br /> <br /> If you treat a Rampant Beast as Lair zero for Atavisms, they become toothless mechanically. So, whether you want to keep to the thematics of the merger, you need to come up with some number so these monsters are worth the classification. If not past Lair, what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T13:12:07-07:00","id":1561141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects?p=1561134#post1561134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was uncertain, but went on because I think it still applies.<br /> <br /> The Lair is relevant because it draws on certain kinds of symbolism that is important to the Beast.<br /> <br /> But when the Horror changes from Beast to something else, anything else, this is a conceptual change in a highly semantic being. Even if their Lair is relevant to say where you're coming from, I'm not sure it should inform a lot on what &quot;you&quot; become.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, but still. they are difficult to play because an inherent part of their powers is without data,i mean, how do other storytellers play atavisms without lair? body warp and rolls based on attributes i understand, but here you are missing a core component of the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T15:19:58-07:00","id":1561144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects?p=1561141#post1561141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense, but still. they are difficult to play because an inherent part of their powers is without data,i mean, how do other storytellers play atavisms without lair? body warp and rolls based on attributes i understand, but here you are missing a core component of the game</div> </div> </div> </div>In practical terms, the Rampant are similar to fully-embodied Hosts from Werewolf \u2014 they don't have a Supernatural Potency rating for mechanical purposes, and while their former Lair rating informs their level of power it doesn't give them any of the other benefits of Lair like Environmental Immunity, Chambers, Primordial Pathways, etc.<br /> <br /> It may help to think of them as mechanically balanced to be threats to mortals and problems and complications to stronger monsters \u2014 they're functionally a way to have loose Atavisms out in the world spreading fear in a material way where the Unfettered wander the Dream and occasionally pop up in stranger spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T16:15:43-07:00","id":1561146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1561098-merged-beast-and-lair-based-atavisms-effects?p=1561140#post1561140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you treat a Rampant Beast as Lair zero for Atavisms, they become toothless mechanically. So, whether you want to keep to the thematics of the merger, you need to come up with some number so these monsters are worth the classification. If not past Lair, what?</div> </div> </div> </div>A made-up number.<br /> <br /> My point isn't to treat as zero or something, is to not fix too much on the previous stats.<br /> <br /> It adds something to the mystique that the resulting monster can't be predicted from the former state, and that Beasts that follow this path may become way tougher (or weaker) threats than they originally were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T16:27:03-07:00","id":1561147,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really resolve the conflict of the stance you're taking. Either:<br /> <br /> 1) The stat is going to be based on something on the character sheet, and thus tied what the Begotten was into what they become (which is already very much the case, Rampant are the Hunger given physical form, so what your Hunger was is what the Rampant will be)<br /> <br /> 2) The stat is going to be disconnected from the Beast, and thus run roughshod over the semantic nature of the character types. Their natures, Lives, and Legends, are fundamental to what paths are open to them; that's how you build up the Lair stat in the first place. <br /> <br /> I could use the rules to generate the Horror's stats as an ephemeral entity, and base Atavisms on Power instead of Lair... but that Power stat is just as narratively derived as Lair is. So is any other number other than something arbitrary and random... which isn't supposed to be part of the way a Beast's story unfolds... they are creatures of narrative not chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}